.TH CONNECT 10 "October 2026" "1.1" "Neverdark Manual"
.SH NAME
connect \- Log in over a raw connection
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B connect
.I name
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
.B connect
is how a raw\-telnet guest logs in. It is a two\-phase command:
.BI connect " name"
arms a one\-shot password prompt on your connection, and the next line you
type is the password. That line is consumed as a password: it is never
echoed, never shown in scrollback, and never run as a command. A name alone
never authenticates.
.PP
The password is checked through the axil\-auth credential store. An unknown
name, a wrong password, and an unavailable authentication service all answer
the same
.IR "Invalid name or password." ,
so the prompt cannot be used to enumerate accounts, and a failed guess closes
the connection: every guess costs a reconnect.
.PP
A brand\-new name creates a player on first login; a known name re\-anchors
the player to the new connection. A WebSocket login never uses this command:
the browser session establishes the identity instead, before any command runs.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR begin,help (10)
.SH AUTHOR
quirinpa <quirinpa@tty.pt>
